{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And see, and make, according to their pattern.</b> From what is seen, it should have said כתבניתם — 'according to (כ) their pattern' — with a kaph, which is the kaph of likeness always found in Scripture regarding things that resemble one another in one respect but not in all. For in truth it was impossible for Moses to make according to the pattern of those things which He was showing on the mountain, for there he saw intelligible, spiritual things, and here he was commanded to make them corporeal. If so, it is impossible to say בתבניתם with a bet, but rather with a kaph, which would be the kaph of likeness, to indicate that there is in them resemblance from one side. <b>And</b> what he mentioned בתבניתם with a bet — it seems to me that the verse's parsing is thus: 'and see בתבניתם — in their pattern — which you are being shown on the mountain, and make,' that is, with your materials. For how could he say בתבניתם, when it is impossible to make according to the pattern of those things exactly? And they are as the Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: for Moses said to the Holy One, blessed be He: do I then have red fire, white fire, green fire, black fire?'" "<b>And</b> you should reflect upon the distinction that exists in the Holy Tongue between bet and kaf — between saying בתבניתם and כתבניתם — and you will know and understand this from what emerges from the cited verse in Genesis: בצלמנו כדמותנו — that regarding צלם he used a bet, and its meaning is that צלם refers to the condition (צורך) of the intellect and the rational soul in man together with the separate intelligences — all are one species, and the need (צורך) among them is one; therefore he said בצלמנו — in that very same צלם. But regarding דמות he used a kaf, for man resembles the likeness of the angels in appearance, but the דמות is not identical among them. From this he said בצלמנו with a bet, כדמותנו with a kaf, and this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:35.504412297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}